  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a persistent upward bias when recent history is volatile and trending down; true outcomes often drop significantly below the forecasted path within the first 5-7 days.",
    "Forecast fails to account for immediate mean reversion after a price spike, instead projecting continued linear growth that ignores the high probability of a sharp reversal in the next 30d horizon.",
    "Sentiment history shows no predictive power for short-term direction; corrections should rely solely on volatility and trend analysis rather than sentiment adjustments.",
    "When recent history ends with a local low (e.g., <62.50), the model overestimates recovery speed, whereas true outcomes frequently retest lower levels before any sustained rise.",
    "The 30d forecast horizon is systematically too optimistic; actual outcomes typically converge to a mean significantly lower than the model's terminal projection by day 15."
  ]
}
